  "prefLabel": "Res 102.04 Division of Parks and Recreation",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Res 102.04 Division of Parks and Recreation.\n\n(a) The division of parks and recreation shall be responsible for managing the state park system, including recreation areas, a state ski area, historic sites, trails, and natural areas under the division's jurisdiction. The director of the division of parks and recreation shall execute all matters pertaining to the administration and operation of recreational facilities and services for public use on lands under the divisions jurisdiction. The division shall consist of 3 bureaus which shall be directly responsible to the director.\n\n(b) The trails bureau shall be responsible for programs relative to off highway recreational vehicles, state-owned multi-purpose recreational trails, the New Hampshire Heritage Trail, and New Hampshire Conservation Corps programs.\n\n(c) The parks bureau shall be responsible for the development, administration and operation of recreational facilities and services for public use on all public areas of recreational significance such as state parks, forests, reservations, and historic sites.\n\n(d) The bureau of state ski operations shall be responsible for managing the year round operations at Cannon Mountain ski area. The bureau shall promote year round tourism promotion and economic development to the regions in proximity to the area and shall strive to provide quality recreational experiences year round to visitors and residents.\n\nSource. #2221, eff 12-23-82; ss by #2979, eff 2-21-85; EXPIRED 2-21-91\n\nNew. #5798, eff 3-18-94, EXPIRED: 3-18-00\n\nNew. #7395, eff 11-1-00, EXPIRED: 7-1-18",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/res100.html"
